[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Behaviour of the intake and pipeline item as built: format detection, archive handling, the row buffer, the
parse cache, the pipeline entry point `run_analysis`, the `flightmd` command line and the package root. Code:
`flightmd_core/services/format_detector.py`, `flightmd_core/services/compressed.py`,
`flightmd_core/services/columns.py`, `flightmd_core/cache.py`, `flightmd_core/orchestrator.py`,
`flightmd_core/__main__.py`, `flightmd_core/__init__.py`. Low-level requirements are in `llr-int.sdoc`, the
design in `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-int.md`, the interface in
`docs/lifecycle/03-system/icd/icd-cli-library.md`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Format detection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Format identified from content
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall identify a log from at most its first 4096 bytes as one of `px4_ulog`, `ardupilot_bin`,
`ardupilot_log`, `mavlink_tlog`, `betaflight_bbl` or `dji_txt`, whatever the file is called, and shall hold one
parser class for each identifier.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unrecognised and unsupported files are refused with a reason
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall refuse a file whose content matches no supported format with an `UnsupportedFormatError` (a
`ValueError`) whose message lists the supported formats, shall give a specific message for a `.log` file that is
not a text dataflash log, and shall refuse a DJI aircraft .DAT file with a message naming the flight record to
upload instead and with `format_id` set to `dji_dat`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The file name is a hint for a short header only
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall use the file extension only when the bytes given are too few to decide and are not the whole
file: a header that could be the start of a MAVLink telemetry log is accepted as `mavlink_tlog` when the name
ends in `.tlog`, and a header that could be the start of a DJI flight record is accepted as `dji_txt` when the
name ends in `.txt`. When the bytes are the whole file the extension decides nothing except the wording of the
refusal.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
COMMENT: >>>
As built, `detect_format` treats a file of 4096 bytes or more as not complete, so a `.txt` file whose first
4096 bytes neither confirm nor rule out a DJI record is still accepted on its extension (LLR-INT-009,
LLR-INT-011).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Compressed uploads

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gzip and zip uploads
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall recognise a gzip file and a zip file by their first bytes, not by name, shall unpack the one log
inside into a private temporary directory, and shall hand back the path of the unpacked log and a function that
removes the directory. A file that is neither is handed back unchanged. In a zip, folders and operating-system
clutter (`__MACOSX/`, `.DS_Store`, `Thumbs.db`, `desktop.ini`) do not count as files.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Archives that are refused
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall refuse with a `ValueError` that says why: a damaged or truncated archive, a zip that does not
hold exactly one file, a zip entry with an absolute path, a drive letter or a `..` component, a password
protected zip member, and an archive whose content is another archive (by member extension or by the first
bytes of the unpacked data). Nothing unpacked is left on disk after a refusal.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test builds a password protected zip; a review checks the flag test in `_zip_source` (LLR-INT-018). The
other refusals are tested.
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded decompression
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall stop unpacking and refuse the archive when the unpacked size passes the byte limit given by the
caller, or passes 200 times the packed file size where that product is above 1 MiB (1 048 576 bytes), and shall
refuse a zip beforehand when the sizes declared in its directory break either limit.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Limits on one analysis

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Input size limit
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis` shall refuse, before reading the content, a file larger than `FLIGHTMD_MAX_LOG_MB` megabytes
(1 MB = 1 000 000 bytes, default 512) with a `ValueError` giving the size and the limit, and shall pass the same
limit in bytes to the unpacking step.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parse time limit
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall parse the log in a separate process and, when the parse has not finished within
`FLIGHTMD_PARSE_TIMEOUT_S` seconds (default 600), shall stop that process and raise a `ValueError` saying the
parse took too long. A parser process that ends without a result is reported as a `ValueError` with its exit
code. A limit of 0 or less parses in the calling process with no time limit.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The timeout and the in-process mode are tested. No test kills the parser process from outside; a review checks
that branch of `_parse_with_limit` (LLR-INT-039).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Numeric settings that cannot be read fall back to the default
STATEMENT: >>>
A numeric environment setting (`FLIGHTMD_MAX_LOG_MB`, `FLIGHTMD_PARSE_TIMEOUT_S`, `FLIGHTMD_CACHE_TTL_S`,
`FLIGHTMD_CACHE_MAX_MB`) whose text is not a number shall be replaced by its default without an error.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for it. It keeps a mistyped setting from stopping every analysis; the limits of
SYS-003 then apply with their default values.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests set valid values only. A review checks the `except ValueError` in both `_env_float` functions. The texts
`nan` and `inf` are numbers to `float` and are not replaced (LLR-INT-033).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Parse cache

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parse kept by SHA-256, for a limited time and size
STATEMENT: >>>
When the cache is on, the item shall keep the parser output (topics, parameters, metadata) of each log in one
file named by the SHA-256 of the uploaded file under `<FLIGHTMD_DATA_DIR>/cache`, shall not use an entry last
written or read more than `FLIGHTMD_CACHE_TTL_S` seconds ago (default 3600), and after each write shall delete
expired entries and then the oldest entries until the total is at most `FLIGHTMD_CACHE_MAX_MB` megabytes (default
1024). The cache is on when `FLIGHTMD_CACHE` says so, or, when that is unset, when `FLIGHTMD_DATA_DIR` is set. A
key that is not 64 lower-case hexadecimal characters is refused.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: An unreadable cache entry is dropped
STATEMENT: >>>
A cache entry that cannot be opened or unpickled shall be deleted and treated as a miss, so the log is parsed
again. Entries are written under a temporary name and renamed, so a reader never sees a partly written entry,
and entries of another cache version are deleted when the cache is pruned.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
COMMENT: >>>
As built only `OSError`, `EOFError`, `pickle.UnpicklingError`, `AttributeError` and `ImportError` are handled;
other errors from a damaged entry leave `cache.get` and the entry stays (LLR-INT-030).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A reused parse gives the same report content
STATEMENT: >>>
The cache entry shall hold the parse only, written before the pipeline adds anything to the metadata except the
detected format and the SHA-256, so that an analysis from a cached parse gives the same findings, score, parse
warnings and detected format as the analysis that wrote it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: The pipeline (run_analysis)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Library entry point
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall offer the coroutine `run_analysis(ulog_path, file_name, file_size, progress_callback=None,
ai_enhancer=None)`, exported from the package root, which returns a `FlightMDReport` and raises `ValueError`
for a log it cannot analyse: too large, unrecognised format, refused archive, parse failure, parse timeout, or
no analysable telemetry.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
COMMENT: >>>
As built, errors raised after the parse (path building, analyser loading, report assembly) and a few before it
are not converted and leave `run_analysis` as their own types (LLD section 4).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A log with no analysable telemetry is refused
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis` shall raise a `ValueError` saying there is nothing to score when the parse holds no topic other
than `vehicle_status` and `vehicle_land_detected` topics.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test in the assigned files reaches this branch. A review checks the topic-name test and the message in
`run_analysis` (LLR-INT-046).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Progress reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis` shall call `progress_callback(pct, message, eta_s)`, which may be a plain function or a
coroutine function, with `pct` an integer from 5 to 100 that never goes down, `message` a short text, and
`eta_s` the estimated seconds left rounded to 0.1 s or `None`. The last call is `(100, "Done.", 0.0)`. An
exception from the callback shall be logged and shall not stop the analysis.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-027
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Armed windows and the notes about them
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall set `metadata.armed_windows` to the list of `[start_s, end_s]` pairs, in log-relative seconds
rounded to 0.001 s, during which `vehicle_status.arming_state` equals 2. When the log has no arming data it
shall set `None` and add the parse warning "No arming information in this log, so the whole recording is
treated as flight."; when the vehicle never armed it shall set an empty list and add "The vehicle never armed
during this log.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The armed and the no-arming-data cases are tested on the sample logs. No test has a log that never arms; a
review checks that branch (LLR-INT-048).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Flight path and derived figures
STATEMENT: >>>
From the GPS receiver topic, or the estimator's global position when the receiver gives no usable fix, the item
shall fill `metadata.gps_path` (latitude and longitude in degrees, altitude in metres) by taking every n-th
point with n = max(1, points // 500), with the time of each point in log-relative seconds and, where logged,
HDOP and wind speed per point. Where the parser left them empty it shall fill the maximum altitude above the
first point, the total distance and the maximum speed, leaving out of distance and speed every segment shorter
than 0.05 s or faster than 75 m/s.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
COMMENT: >>>
As built the sampling gives up to 999 points, not 500, and implausible points stay on the path; only distance
and speed leave them out (LLR-INT-051, LLR-INT-052).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The metadata names the input
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall set `metadata.log_sha256` to the SHA-256 of the file as given to `run_analysis` (before any
decompression) and `metadata.source_format` to the detected format identifier, and shall pass `file_name` and
`file_size` as given to the report builder.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Flight context and offline mode
STATEMENT: >>>
When `FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE` is `1`, `true`, `yes` or `on`, `run_analysis` shall make no weather, place-name or AI
call. `metadata.weather` shall always be set: to the looked-up weather when online with a position and a log
date, otherwise to empty values with the reason in `description` (no GPS position, offline mode, or flight date
unknown). The place name is looked up when online with a position.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The offline case is tested. The test suite never goes online; a review checks the online branches
(LLR-INT-054).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-025
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Every analyser is run or reported as skipped, in a fixed order
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall load the analysers after the metadata is complete, run through `safe_analyse` each one whose
inputs are present, take a skip result from each one whose inputs are missing, and pass the results on in a
fixed order: the run analysers in registry order, then the skipped ones in registry order.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Score, explanations and the limit on the AI
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall compute the score before the summary, have the explanation engine explain every finding and
write the summary, and if that engine fails shall give each unexplained finding its technical summary as the
explanation with a fixed recommendation and write a fixed-form summary. An AI enhancer shall be called only
when one is given, is configured and the item is not offline, and only its returned summary text shall be used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The normal path is tested end to end on the sample logs. No test in the assigned files makes the explanation
engine fail or passes an enhancer; a review checks those branches (LLR-INT-057, LLR-INT-058).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-023

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Command line

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: flightmd analyse
STATEMENT: >>>
`flightmd analyse LOG [--json FILE] [--pdf FILE] [--gpx FILE] [--kml FILE] [--offline | --online]` (the word
`analyse` may be left out) shall analyse one log, write each export asked for through a `.part` file that is
renamed, print the file name, score, grade, label, parse warnings and finding titles on standard output, and
return 0. It shall return 2 when the log file does not exist, 1 with `error: <reason>` on standard error when
the log cannot be analysed, and 3 when the PDF cannot be rendered (the other exports are still written).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Exit codes 0, 1 and 3 and the exports are tested. No test passes a missing file; a review checks that branch
(LLR-INT-062).
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The command line is offline unless asked otherwise
STATEMENT: >>>
`flightmd analyse` shall set `FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE` to `1` when neither flag is given and the variable is not
already set, to `1` with `--offline` and to `0` with `--online`, and shall never pass an AI enhancer.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test runs `flightmd analyse` and checks the offline setting it leaves (LLR-INT-062 is reviewed, not tested).
A review reads `analyse` in `__main__.py` for the three cases: no flag, `--offline`, `--online`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: flightmd compare
STATEMENT: >>>
`flightmd compare BEFORE AFTER` shall read two report JSON files and print the two file names, the overall
scores and their difference, each module whose score changed or is missing on one side, the titles of findings
present only in the first report as `resolved:` and only in the second as `new:`, and return 0. A file that
cannot be read or is not JSON gives `error: can't read <file>: <reason>` and exit code 2.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
COMMENT: >>>
As built a report without a numeric `overall_score` ends the command with an uncaught `TypeError`, and a "Not
assessed" report is compared as score 0 (LLR-INT-067, LLR-INT-068).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-027

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Supporting parts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Row buffer for numeric columns
STATEMENT: >>>
The item shall offer `ColumnBuffer`, which takes rows of numbers one at a time under fixed, distinct column
names, stores them as 64-bit floats with `None` as NaN, refuses a value that is not a number, and gives the rows
back as one table.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for it. It is the storage the dataflash and telemetry parsers use so that a log of
tens of millions of values fits in memory; it supports the common internal model of SYS-004.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Package root
STATEMENT: >>>
The package `flightmd_core` shall export `run_analysis`, `FlightMDReport`, `Finding`, `AnalyserResult`,
`ParamRecommendation`, `Severity`, `Category` and `FlightMetadata`, and states its version as
`__version__ = "1.0.0"`.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The exported names serve SYS-027. No Active system requirement asks for the version attribute; it is recorded
because the corpus goldens store it. It differs from the version in `pyproject.toml` (1.1.0).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test asserts the exported names or the version value. A review reads `flightmd_core/__init__.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-INT-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Real-log regression corpus check
STATEMENT: >>>
The corpus test shall run each log of `tests/corpus/manifest.json` through `run_analysis` offline, after
checking the file against the manifest SHA-256, and shall fail when, against that log's golden file, the score
leaves the stored band, the set of finding kinds with severities or the set of assessed modules differs, a
stored metric is missing or outside tolerance, or the stored metadata differs. It runs only when asked for
(`pytest -m corpus`), and the manifest shall hold 10 to 20 well-formed entries.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Verified at this level only: the requirement is implemented by test code (`tests/corpus/test_corpus.py`),
which the trace does not tag. LLR-INT-071 and LLR-INT-072 record what is compared and with what tolerance.
<<<
ALLOCATION: tools, procedure
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-038

